  "description": "Plakar uses native FastCDC around 1 MiB and LZ4 stream compression, with plaintext storage. Gutch uses a nominal 1 MiB FastCDC target, LZ4 0 and 8 MiB compressed bundles. Bounds, compression units/framing and packing differ. Plakar restores over existing output; this adapter has no native extra-file deletion. Fresh repositories and isolated caches. Four workers where exposed; native Borg/BPT scheduling. One warm-up and 6 rotating measured repetitions; profiling off. Measurement contract 2 separates content repair, preserved-mtime damage, extra-file cleanup and full restoration. Strict source-derived SHA-256 validation follows every supported operation; both native and validation-inclusive durations are reported. Unsupported operations receive no timing.",
